        quote: "Al-Hubab ibn al-Mundhir, an expert tactician, stepped forward respectfully: 'O Messenger of Allah, is this position a divine revelation which we cannot alter, or is it military opinion, warfare, and strategy?' The Prophet ﷺ answered: 'Rather, it is opinion, warfare, and strategy!' Hubab advised: 'Then this is not the right place! Advance the army to the nearest spring to the enemy, fill the remaining wells, and dig a reservoir so we drink while they cannot.' The Prophet ﷺ immediately agreed: 'You have spoken sound strategy!' and relocated the army.",
        moralLesson: "Participatory leadership (Shura): separating divine dogma from practical technical matters, and joyfully embracing expert counsel from subordinates.",
